  "assumptions": [
    "Preserve all already-earned starting resources in every variant; changes are prospective.",
    "Current and compact variants use identical real 7-group rotation, targets, eligibility, grants and receipts.",
    "Simple candidate: one daily three-distinct-board goal, no rotating metric; milestone payments 10/10/40, same maximum 60. It is NOT implemented in gameplay.",
    "Off candidate removes only future quest income; Daily 30, unique-board coins, rank and workshop remain unchanged.",
    "Same solved-ID trace in each variant; quest-guided traces do not predict what a person would choose under another policy.",
    "Income uses no-help actual settlements; help expenses are a sensitivity model, not an ad impression or a behavioural forecast.",
    "Help is paid before a board; ordinary income afterwards; weekly prizes after closing the week, available in subsequent weeks only.",
    "An unfunded request assumes one external earned credit to continue the fixed trace; no automatic game grant or live SDK claim.",
    "Zero baseline income has no finite percentage: report absolute coins/help capacity, never divide by zero.",
    "Weekly A/B/C remain unchanged proposals; D is an additional lower coin-only proposal. No runtime policy, payout or economy change."
